        "meaning": "Summarize a coherent lesson with actual student reasoning at its center.",
        "example": "Students first identify the unknown and model the temperature change independently. I then connect their approaches or labeled teacher examples to missing-addend reasoning, subtraction, and addition of the opposite. Partners critique equation cards with reciprocal roles, the whole group compares forward/reverse change, and each learner independently solves the sensor task and describes a check.",
        "why": "The sequence makes prior ideas visible, teaches a connection, and checks transfer after collaboration.",
